ok   a text result set decodes every column type
ok   text values have the Ruby classes of their column types, strings UTF-8 except binary columns
ok   a prepared statement's binary rows decode to the same values as the text protocol
ok   COM_STMT_EXECUTE lays out the NULL bitmap, the types and each bind's value
ok   what the bound row holds, read back
ok   binary rows of 7, 8 and 9 columns place each NULL bit after the two reserved bits
ok   a text row of 9 columns with NULLs
ok   OK packets give affected_rows and last_insert_id in each length encoding
ok   a multi-statement query answers its last result
ok   an ERR in the second statement raises, and the connection carries on
ok   each recorded ERR maps to its DB::Error class with the server's message, code and state
ok   the codes MySQL 8 did not send map too
ok   a lost connection is ConnectionLost
ok   KILL QUERY interrupts SLEEP, which answers 1
ok   a failed prepare raises the mapped error
ok   execute refuses a wrong bind count and an unknown statement before sending anything
ok   close_statement sends COM_STMT_CLOSE and forgets the statement
ok   ping answers true for OK and false when the connection is gone; quit sends COM_QUIT
ok   a BIGINT UNSIGNED past 2**63 - 1 is refused once the result is read, in both protocols
ok   zero dates decode as zeros in both protocols
